Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer, New Grad* role at *Notion*. My strongest match is building product features from conception through implementation and maintenance across the full stack. At Sperse, I planned and shipped TypeScript, Node.js, React Flow, Python, and FastAPI experiences that let more than 10,000 users create and manage durable agentic workflows. I paired those interfaces with backend systems, secure access controls, and resilient execution, focusing on successful systems and user impact rather than technology for its own sake.

I have also improved performance and reliability and built internal tools that make teams more productive. I added live Redis progress tracking to long-running Temporal workflows so users could understand execution state and recover cleanly. I integrated Codex with a custom Bitbucket MCP server to automate triage across 25–30 pull requests each week, saving reviewers several hours, and built GitHub Actions and OpenTelemetry pipelines to catch latency, accuracy, and safety regressions before production. Earlier at Qualitest, I developed backend services with Java, Spring Boot, PostgreSQL, and Redis, optimized database models with window functions, materialized views, and indexes, and delivered React interfaces for business stakeholders.

Notion's mission to make software toolmaking ubiquitous resonates with how I approach engineering: build adaptable tools that help people solve real problems. I am especially drawn to the values of keeping the customer in every room and owning the outcome. My Dark Factory project reflects that builder mindset by decomposing tricky requests into dependency-aware task DAGs and coordinating collaborative AI agents through maintainable, observable workflows. Across my work, I use AI-assisted development tools such as Codex and Claude Code pragmatically while staying responsible for product judgment, system quality, and the human impact of what I build.

I would welcome the opportunity to help Notion shape and polish quality web applications, improve activation and reliability, and create internal tools that give customers and teammates more time for their life's work. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

